BCC_Q({"lv": "910", "y": 2024, "n": 13, "part": "C", "topic": "algo", "title": "Floor Patterns", "answer": 3, "story": "<p>A machine uses gates to redirect a sequence of balls in order to\nproduce a pattern on the floor when viewed from above. Each ball follows\na path directed by the gates. After a ball passes through a gate, the\ngate switches direction, sending the next ball the other way, as shown\nbelow.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"A description of the\ndiagram follows.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:800px\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>\n<button onclick=\"hideSeek('longdesc3')\" style=\"box-shadow: none;\">Hide/Reveal Description of Diagram for Floor Patterns<\/button>\n<div id=\"longdesc3\" style=\"display: none;\">\n<p>Three images on a row of a vertical path splitting into a left and a right\npath at a gate. Arrows point from one image to the next.<\/p>\n<p>The first image shows a ball with a yellow square approaching the\ngate and a ball with a blue circle and a red rectangle following it. The\ngate is placed so the left path is open and the right path is closed.<\/p>\n<p>The second image shows the ball with a yellow square in the left\npath, past the gate, and the other ball approaching the gate. The gate\nis placed so the right path is open and the left path is closed.<\/p>\n<p>The third image shows the ball with a blue circle and a red rectangle\nin the right path, past the gate. The gate is placed so the left path is\nopen and the right path is closed.<\/p>\n<hr class=\"longdesc\"/><\/div>\n<p>In the example above, the gate initially opens to the left, sending\nthe first ball left. As the first ball goes through the gate, it causes\nthe gate to switch so that it will send the next ball to the right. As\nthe second ball goes through the gate, it causes the gate to switch back\nagain.<\/p>\n<p>Every ball is labelled with one or more shapes. When a ball hits the\nfloor, the pattern produced on the floor is triple the shape(s) shown on\nthat ball. When two or more balls land at the same location, their\npatterns will combine on the floor. The pattern created on the floor by\nthe example above is shown below.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"Three yellow squares are scattered on the left side of the floor and a mixture of three blue circles and three red rectangles are scattered on the right side of the floor.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:300px\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>", "question": "<p>Which sequence of balls will create the following pattern on the\nfloor?<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"A mixture of three yellow squares and three blue circles are scattered on the left side of the floor. Six pink triangles are scattered in the middle of the floor. A mixture of three yellow squares and three red rectangles are scattered on the right side of the floor.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:550px\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>\n<ol class=\"mc\">\n<li><p> <img alt=\"A description of Options\nA through D follows.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:250px\"/> <\/p><\/li>\n<li><p> <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:250px\"/> <\/p><\/li>\n<li><p> <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:250px\"/> <\/p><\/li>\n<li><p> <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:250px\"/> <\/p><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<button onclick=\"hideSeek('longdesc4')\" style=\"box-shadow: none;\">Hide/Reveal Descriptions of Options A - D for Floor\nPatterns<\/button>\n<div id=\"longdesc4\" style=\"display: none;\">\n<p>Each of Options A through D show the same path and gate\nstructure: A vertical path divides into a left path and right path at a\ntop gate. Then the left path divides again into a left and right path at\na bottom left gate and the right path divides again into a left and\nright path at a bottom right gate. The two paths in the middle merge so\nthat only three paths exit the gate structure. Each of the three gates\nare initially placed so that the path to the left is open and the path\nto the right is closed.<\/p>\n<ol type=\"A\">\n<li><p>Option A has four balls lined up at the top gate. Starting with\nthe ball closest to the top gate and moving away, the balls have the\nfollowing shapes:\n<ol start=\"1\" type=\"1\">\n<li>a blue circle and a yellow square<\/li>\n<li>a pink triangle<\/li>\n<li>a red rectangle and a yellow square<\/li>\n<li>a pink triangle<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li><p>Option B has five balls lined up at the top gate. Starting with\nthe ball closest to the top gate and moving away, the balls have the\nfollowing shapes:\n<ol start=\"1\" type=\"1\">\n<li>a yellow square<\/li>\n<li>a pink triangle<\/li>\n<li>a red rectangle<\/li>\n<li>a blue circle and a yellow square<\/li>\n<li>a pink triangle<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li><p>Option C has three balls lined up at the top gate. Starting\nwith the ball closest to the top gate and moving away, the balls have\nthe following shapes:\n<ol start=\"1\" type=\"1\">\n<li>a blue circle and a yellow square<\/li>\n<li>a pink triangle<\/li>\n<li>a red rectangle and a yellow square<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li><p>Option D has five balls lined up at the top gate. Starting with\nthe ball closest to the top gate and moving away, the balls have the\nfollowing shapes:\n<ol start=\"1\" type=\"1\">\n<li>a blue circle<\/li>\n<li>a pink triangle<\/li>\n<li>a pink triangle<\/li>\n<li>a red rectangle and a yellow square<\/li>\n<li>a yellow square<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<hr class=\"longdesc\"/><\/div>", "answerHtml": "<p>(D) <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:250px\"/> <\/p>", "explanation": "<p>The following diagram shows how Option D creates the desired\npattern.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"A description of the\ndiagram follows.\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:100%\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>\n<button onclick=\"hideSeek('longdesc5')\" style=\"box-shadow: none;\">Hide/Reveal Description of Diagram for Floor Patterns\nExplanation<\/button>\n<div id=\"longdesc5\" style=\"display: none;\">\n<p>Five images in a row of the gate structure with five balls from\nOption (D) at five different stages.<\/p>\n<p>Stage 1: The first ball, with a blue circle, moves left at the top\ngate and then left at the bottom left gate and exits via the leftmost\npath. This results in three blue circles on the left side of the floor.\nAlso, the top gate rotates to open its right path, as does the bottom\nleft gate.<\/p>\n<p>Stage 2: The second ball, with a pink triangle, moves right at the\ntop gate and then left at the bottom right gate and exits via the middle\npath. This results in three pink triangles in the middle of the floor.\nAlso, the top gate rotates to open its left path and the bottom right\ngate rotates to open its right path.<\/p>\n<p>Stage 3: The third ball, with a pink triangle, moves left at the top\ngate and then right at the bottom left gate and exits via the middle\npath. This results in three more pink triangles in the middle of the\nfloor. Also, the top gate rotates to open its right path and the bottom\nleft gate rotates to open its left path.<\/p>\n<p>Stage 4: The fourth ball, with a red rectangle and a yellow square,\nmoves right at the top gate and then right at the bottom right gate and\nexits via the rightmost path. This results in three red rectangles and\nthree yellow squares on the right side of the floor. Also, the top gate\nrotates to open its left path, as does the bottom right gate.<\/p>\n<p>Stage 5: The fifth ball, with a yellow square, moves left at the top\ngate and then left at the bottom left gate and exits via the leftmost\npath. This results in three yellow squares in the left side of the\nfloor. Also, the top gate rotates to open its right path, as does the\nbottom left gate.<\/p>\n<hr class=\"longdesc\"/><\/div>\n<p>Option A is incorrect because it will create the following\npattern.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"Three yellow squares and three blue circles\non the left, three pink triangles, three red rectangles and three yellow\nsquares in the middle, and three pink triangles on the right.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:550px\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>Option B is incorrect because it will create the following\npattern.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"Three yellow squares and three pink triangles\non the left, three pink triangles and three red rectangles in the\nmiddle, and three blue circles and three yellow squares on the\nright.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:550px\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>Option C is incorrect because it will create the following\npattern.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"Three yellow squares and three blue circles\non the left, three pink triangles, three red rectangles and three yellow\nsquares in the middle, and no shapes on the right.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:550px\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>", "connections": "<p>Computer chips, such as the <em>central processing unit (CPU)<\/em> or\n<em>random access memory (RAM)<\/em> are built using extremely small\nelectrical components known as <em>transistors<\/em>. A transistor can be\nthought of as a switch, which can be opened (or \"on\" or \"1\") if there is\nelectrical current applied to it, or closed (or \"off\" of \"0\") if there\nis no electrical current. Combining multiple transistors together allows\ncomputers to store more information, such as a sequence of binary\nnumbers, or <em>bits<\/em>.<\/p>\n<p>In this task, each gate represents a transistor, which can be \"on\"\n(meaning the next ball will fall to the left) or \"off\" (meaning the next\nball will fall to the right).<\/p>\n<p>Modern <em>microchips<\/em> are composed of millions of transistors\npacked into an area that is less than 2cm by 2cm.<\/p>"});